---
---
<section id="fit-guide" class="py-10 sm:py-16 md:py-24 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-5xl mx-auto border-t border-hairline">
  <div class="mb-8 sm:mb-12 text-center md:text-left">
    <span class="inline-block py-1 px-3 rounded-full bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary mb-3">
      Fit Diagnostic
    </span>
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Fit Diagnostic & Solutions</h2>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-lg text-body max-w-2xl">
      A calculated size is a starting point. Your bra should fit comfortably without digging or slipping. Diagnose common fit issues below.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- How to Know if Your Bra Fits Correctly (3 Pillars of Fit) -->
  <div class="mb-10 sm:mb-14">
    <div class="mb-6">
      <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-2">How to Know if Your Bra Fits Correctly</h3>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-body">
        Before troubleshooting specific issues, check these 3 key areas to confirm an ideal fit.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <!-- The Cups -->
      <div class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-xs flex flex-col justify-between hover:border-hairline-strong transition-all duration-200">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline text-primary flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.318 6.318a4.5 4.5 0 000 6.364L12 20.364l7.682-7.682a4.5 4.5 0 00-6.364-6.364L12 7.636l-1.318-1.318a4.5 4.5 0 00-6.364 0z" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink">1. The Cups</h4>
          </div>
          <div class="mb-4 rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-hairline shadow-2xs aspect-[4/3]">
            <img src="/img/bra-cup-fit-guide.jpg" alt="Bra Cup Fit Visual Guide: Correct vs Incorrect Fit" class="w-full h-full object-cover" />
          </div>
          <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-body">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">✓</span>
              <span>Encapsulates your breasts smoothly with no top or side spillage or gaping.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">✓</span>
              <span>Cups sit flush against tissue with no creases, extra space, or wrinkles.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- The Band -->
      <div class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-xs flex flex-col justify-between hover:border-hairline-strong transition-all duration-200">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline text-primary flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 11H5m14 0a2 2 0 012 2v6a2 2 0 01-2 2H5a2 2 0 01-2-2v-6a2 2 0 012-2m14 0V9a2 2 0 00-2-2M5 11V9a2 2 0 012-2m0 0V5a2 2 0 012-2h6a2 2 0 012 2v2M7 7h10" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink">2. The Band</h4>
          </div>
          <div class="mb-4 rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-hairline shadow-2xs aspect-[4/3]">
            <img src="/img/bra-band-fit-guide.jpg" alt="Bra Band Fit Visual Guide: Level Band vs Riding Up" class="w-full h-full object-cover" />
          </div>
          <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-body">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">✓</span>
              <span>Sits level and snug flat against your body with no digging or loose slack.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">✓</span>
              <span>Feels firm & secure on the <strong class="text-ink font-semibold">loosest hook</strong>, without riding up your back.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- The Straps -->
      <div class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-xs flex flex-col justify-between hover:border-hairline-strong transition-all duration-200">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline text-primary flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 4.354a4 4 0 110 5.292M15 21H3v-1a6 6 0 0112 0v1zm0 0h6v-1a6 6 0 00-9-5.197M13 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0z" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink">3. The Straps</h4>
          </div>
          <div class="mb-4 rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-hairline shadow-2xs aspect-[4/3]">
            <img src="/img/bra-strap-fit-guide.jpg" alt="Bra Strap Fit Visual Guide: Comfortable vs Slipping or Digging" class="w-full h-full object-cover" />
          </div>
          <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-body">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">✓</span>
              <span>Comfortably stay in place on shoulders with no slipping or digging.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">✓</span>
              <span>Takes only ~10-20% of bust weight (the band provides the main support).</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-2">Common Fit Issues & Fixes</h3>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-body">Experiencing discomfort? Select your issue below to see quick solutions.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-4 mb-8 sm:mb-12">
    <details class="group bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-xl p-4 sm:p-6 cursor-pointer hover:border-hairline-strong transition-all duration-200 shadow-xs">
      <summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-bold text-base md:text-lg text-ink list-none">
        <span class="pr-2">The band is riding up my back</span>
        <span class="transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180 text-primary flex-shrink-0">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 text-body text-sm md:text-base pt-4 border-t border-hairline leading-relaxed">
        <p>If the band rides up, it is too loose. The band should sit level around your ribcage. <strong class="text-ink font-semibold">Fix:</strong> Try a tighter sister size (e.g., if you wear 36C, try 34D).</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-xl p-4 sm:p-6 cursor-pointer hover:border-hairline-strong transition-all duration-200 shadow-xs">
      <summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-bold text-base md:text-lg text-ink list-none">
        <span class="pr-2">My straps keep falling off</span>
        <span class="transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180 text-primary flex-shrink-0">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 text-body text-sm md:text-base pt-4 border-t border-hairline leading-relaxed">
        <p>This often happens when the band is too loose, causing the straps to sit too far apart on your shoulders. <strong class="text-ink font-semibold">Fix:</strong> First, tighten the straps. If that fails, go down a band size and up a cup size.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-xl p-4 sm:p-6 cursor-pointer hover:border-hairline-strong transition-all duration-200 shadow-xs">
      <summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-bold text-base md:text-lg text-ink list-none">
        <span class="pr-2">My breasts are bulging out (spillage)</span>
        <span class="transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180 text-primary flex-shrink-0">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 text-body text-sm md:text-base pt-4 border-t border-hairline leading-relaxed">
        <p>If there is spillage at the top or sides, the cup is too small. <strong class="text-ink font-semibold">Fix:</strong> Keep your band size the same, but increase the cup size (e.g., 34B to 34C).</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-xl p-4 sm:p-6 cursor-pointer hover:border-hairline-strong transition-all duration-200 shadow-xs">
      <summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-bold text-base md:text-lg text-ink list-none">
        <span class="pr-2">There are gaps in the cups</span>
        <span class="transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180 text-primary flex-shrink-0">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 text-body text-sm md:text-base pt-4 border-t border-hairline leading-relaxed">
        <p>If there is space between your breast and the cup, the cup is too large or the style doesn't suit your breast shape. <strong class="text-ink font-semibold">Fix:</strong> Try going down a cup size (e.g., 34D to 34C).</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>

  <!-- Contextual Link Callout Box -->
  <div class="p-5 sm:p-6 bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4 text-center sm:text-left shadow-xs">
    <div>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Still unsure about your size?</p>
      <p class="text-xs text-body mt-0.5">Re-check your tape measurements or calculate your starting baseline.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
      <a href="/#how-to-measure" class="px-4 py-2 bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline text-ink text-xs font-semibold rounded-xl hover:bg-hairline transition-colors">
        Measurement Instructions &rarr;
      </a>
      <a href="/#calculator" class="px-4 py-2 bg-primary text-white text-xs font-bold rounded-xl hover:bg-primary-hover transition-colors shadow-2xs">
        Recalculate Bra Size
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  details > summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
</style>
